// Module 3 — CloutHaus: Social Media leads to Compromise
// Workspace: kc7001.eastus/CloutHaus
// Queries replayed on 2026-10-21. Section 1 queries are the ones KC7 prints in the
// question text; Section 2 queries were constructed from the table schema and the
// in-game hints, then verified against the known answers.

// --- Section 1: Got Clout? ---

// Step 1 — Afomiya's employee record: email, username, role, MFA status
// Result: 1 row — afomiya_storm@clouthaus.com, username afstorm, role "Influencer
// Partner", mfa_enabled: False
Employees
| where name contains "afomiya"

// Step 2 — the phishing email impersonating Dior
// Result: 2 rows. Sender collabs@dior-partners.com, subject "[EXTERNAL] Exclusive
// Partnership Opportunity with Dior", verdict CLEAN, link
// https://super-brand-offer.com/login
Email
| where recipient == "afomiya_storm@clouthaus.com"
| where subject contains "dior" or links contains "dior"

// Step 3 — confirm Afomiya clicked the phishing link
// Result: 2 rows, first click at 2025-04-03T11:20:00Z from her own IP (10.10.0.3)
OutboundNetworkEvents
| where url contains "super-brand-offer.com"

// Step 4 — pivot from the phishing domain to its hosting IP
// Result: 198.51.100.12
PassiveDns
| where domain contains "super-brand-offer.com"

// Step 5 — pivot back from that IP to every domain it has ever hosted
// Result: 3 domains — super-brand-offer.com, dior-partners.com, influencer-deals.net
// (the same infrastructure reappears later as the exfiltration destination)
PassiveDns
| where ip contains "198.51.100.12"
| distinct domain

// --- Section 2: Inside the Clout Breach ---
// No query is printed by KC7 for this section — only narrative hints. These were
// built from the table schema (via "View Tables") and verified against the known
// answers before being used in the write-up.

// Step 6 — find the suspicious login to Afomiya's company email
// Result: among 11 logins for "afstorm", one stands out: 2025-04-03T12:20:00Z
// (~1h after the phishing click), hostname MAIL-SERVER01 (not her usual
// OQPA-DESKTOP), src_ip 182.45.67.89, user_agent "MSIE 5.0; Windows NT 5.2",
// result "Successful Login"
AuthenticationEvents
| where username == "afstorm"

// Step 7 — pivot the attacker's login IP to its known domains
// Result: same 3 domains as Step 5 — confirms shared attacker infrastructure
PassiveDns
| where ip contains "182.45.67.89"
| distinct domain

// Step 8 — attacker's reconnaissance against the CloutHaus site
// Result: 27 rows from 182.45.67.89, all MSIE 5.0. Search terms recovered include
// "...Afomiya's email+address??", "...Venmo history - is that public??", and
// "How much would it cost to hire Afomiya for a fake birthday party?"
InboundNetworkEvents
| where src_ip == "182.45.67.89"

// Step 9 — auto-forwarding rule exfiltrating Afomiya's mailbox
// Result: 21 rows, all sender == reply_to == afomiya_storm@clouthaus.com,
// recipient noreply@influencer-deals.net. Subjects include "[EXTERNAL] [FORWARD]
// Afomiya's payment details – direct deposit form" and "...passport scan –
// confidential" (both confirmed below), plus bank statement and tax-document
// forwards per the question text.
Email
| where recipient == "noreply@influencer-deals.net"
